@startuml
title Player-Role (Role Object / DCI)

skinparam legendBackgroundColor #f9f9f9
skinparam legendBorderColor #999999

legend right

**Intent**:
Allow objects (Players) to dynamically acquire/drop roles at runtime without changing the player’s class.

**Motivation**:
Context-dependent behavior (e.g., user roles, game character roles).

**Applicability**:
Context-driven behavior changes; avoid subclass explosion; runtime role attachment.

**Participants**:
Player holds current roles; Role provides behaviors.

**Consequence**:
Pros: Runtime flexibility; separation of concerns; context clarity.
Cons: Complexity in role lifecycle; discoverability of behavior.

**Implementation Notes**:
Use composition over inheritance; roles can be stateful; guard role conflicts.

**Known Uses**:
DCI architecture examples (ata-Context-Interaction); RBAC systems; game engines (character roles/perks).

**Related Patterns**:
Strategy (algorithm role), State (internal role changes), Decorator (attach behavior).

endlegend

class Player {
  -roles : Map<String, Role>
  +attach(role: Role)
  +detach(roleName: String)
  +perform(action: String)
}

interface Role {
  +supports(action: String) : boolean
  +execute(player: Player, action: String)
}

class AdminRole
class GuestRole
class EditorRole

Role <|.. AdminRole
Role <|.. GuestRole
Role <|.. EditorRole

Player o-- Role : dynamic composition
@enduml